# LOCAL.md -- repo facts for the github-workflow skill

<!--
  HOW TO USE THIS FILE

  Copy it to LOCAL.md in this same directory, fill in every <placeholder>,
  and commit LOCAL.md to your repo.

  Ownership contract:

  - LOCAL.md is REPO-OWNED. Provisioning NEVER writes or overwrites
    LOCAL.md -- it only ships and refreshes this LOCAL.md.example.
  - The github-workflow SKILL.md (a sibling file) is MANAGED: provisioning
    overwrites it freely. Never put repo facts there; they belong here.
  - Agents treat LOCAL.md as authoritative for everything listed below.
-->

## Repository Details

- Owner: <owner>
- Repository: <repo>
- Default Branch: <default-branch>

## Remote Topology

<!-- Pick exactly one: direct-origin (origin is the canonical repo; PRs
     open and merge on origin) or fork-upstream (origin is your personal
     fork; the canonical repo is the upstream remote; two-stage PR flow). -->

- Topology: <direct-origin | fork-upstream>
- Upstream: <org>/<repo> <!-- fork-upstream only; the canonical repo where
  Stage-2 PRs live. Leave blank for direct-origin. -->
- Notes: <e.g. "origin is canonical; no upstream remote" or "origin is the
  personal fork of <org>/<repo>; Stage-2 PRs live on the Upstream slug">

## Branch Prefixes

- Human: <user>/feat/..., <user>/fix/..., <user>/refactor/..., <user>/docs/...
- Agent: <agent-prefix>/feat/..., <agent-prefix>/fix/... <!-- often set by
  the harness; humans should not push to agent-prefixed branches -->

## Review Cadence Overrides

<!-- Optional. Overrides the review-watch loop's default wake timings,
     e.g. a machine-global maximum wake interval. Leave blank to use the
     skill defaults. -->

- Max wake interval: <e.g. 240s>

